<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Profit from a River Cruise</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02537</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Profit from a River Cruise</md:title>
    <md:uuid>f9ba8515-b0b8-4af8-b1b9-304c4ff78374</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>A travel company uses a quadratic function to model the profit, in dollars, that it expects to earn from selling tickets to a river cruise at \(d\) dollars per person. The expression \(-d^2+100d-900\) defines this function.</para>
<para>Without graphing, find the price that would generate the maximum profit. Then, determine that maximum profit.</para></section>
</content>
</document>
